# backtrack — success
#
# Going back by a known way. The field is walked out of into the yard; from the yard the field is a
# place already stood in, so its observation says so, `move` is no longer offered on it and
# `backtrack` is in its place. Past the dice the location map asks where to go back to; the field is
# chosen by name, and the walk back follows the known way.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Yard"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# Out to the yard: a way the party does not know yet, so it is walked.
strategy succeed
goal move
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-verb move
expect Moved to: Test Yard

# From the yard the field is known: the observation says so, and going back replaces walking.
observe "Test Field"
click button
advance 12 180
expect I have been there before
goal backtrack
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions
expect go back by the test field

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
wait
expect-state where Test Yard
regions
state
click area Test Field
advance 12 180

expect SUCCESS
expect Moved to: Test Field
expect-verb backtrack
expect-outcome area_move
inspect map
expect-state map walk from Test Yard to Test Field
expect-state map via=line
quit
